# Line motion: ctrl+a / ctrl+e (bubbles/v2 textarea's DefaultKeyMap
# LineStart/LineEnd, bound through internal/tui/editor/model.go's
# KeyLineStart/KeyLineEnd). Verified behaviourally: moving the cursor and
# then inserting a marker proves where the cursor landed.
#
# Word motion (alt+left/right) is not driven here: under kiln's kitty
# keyboard protocol, Orca's synthetic Option/Ctrl+arrow events reach kiln
# without their modifier, while a physical keypress works (checked by hand;
# qa/findings kitty-mode-drops-arrow-modifiers). internal/tui/editor's
# model_test.go covers the alt-arrow bindings.
@faux testdata/faux/hello.yaml
@size 120x40

WAITFOR /describe a task/ 20
TYPE hello world
KEY ctrl+a
TYPE START
SHOT line-start-ctrl-a
EXPECT /STARThello world/
KEY ctrl+e
TYPE END
SHOT line-end-ctrl-e
EXPECT /STARThello worldEND/
EXPECT_NOT /panic|goroutine/
